    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\n\n| Property | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Method | `doInBackground` |\n| Class | `org.fossify.gallery.asynctasks.GetMediaAsynctask` |\n| File | `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/asynctasks/GetMediaAsynctask.kt` |\n| Specification | `DeprecatedApiSpec` |\n\n## Summary\n\n### Reported finding\n\nThe finding (`DeprecatedApiSpec`) reported for `org.fossify.gallery.asynctasks.GetMediaAsynctask.doInBackground`:\n\n> android.os.AsyncTask is deprecated. Use java.util.concurrent or Kotlin Coroutines.\n\n### Root cause\n\nGetMediaAsynctask directly subclasses and uses the deprecated android.os.AsyncTask API (CLM-001). The detector rendered a deprecation message, and the reviewed source confirms the reported deprecated-API predicate.\n\n### Correction strategy\n\nRemove android.os.AsyncTask rather than retaining its UI-thread creation and execute preconditions. Use the repository-selected single-thread executor for serial off-caller-thread work and a main-thread Handler or runOnUiThread mechanism for completion dispatch; retain a cancellable task handle and the existing MediaFetcher.shouldStop signal. This preserves the CONTRACT invariants of serial execution, worker isolation, main-thread results, cancellation, and isolated interrupts (CLM-005, CLM-006, CLM-007).\n\n### Coordinated changes\n\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/asynctasks/GetMediaAsynctask.kt`: Removes the deprecated AsyncTask lifecycle. A companion-owned single-thread executor preserves serial task ordering; the retained FutureTask supplies interruption-capable cancellation and rethrows worker failures from its done callback so they are not silently captured in an unread Future. Handler delivery is gated under the same lock used by stopFetching, preventing queued or already-computed results from invoking the callback after cancellation. start is internal because all coordinated callers are Kotlin within this module, avoiding the previously rejected public API expansion while preserving a single-start IllegalStateException contract.\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/activities/MediaActivity.kt`: Uses the replacement task abstraction's start() launch contract while preserving the retained task instance for existing stopFetching cancellation and retaining the callback behavior unchanged.\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/activities/SearchActivity.kt`: Calls the replacement task abstraction's start() entry point instead of AsyncTask.execute(), while preserving the retained cancellation handle and existing callback behavior.\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/activities/ViewPagerActivity.kt`: Uses GetMediaAsynctask.start(), the replacement launch entry point supplied by the coordinated task migration, instead of deprecated AsyncTask.execute(). The callback contract and refresh-position behavior are unchanged.\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/dialogs/PickMediumDialog.kt`: Uses the replacement GetMediaAsynctask.start() launch entry point supplied by the coordinated task migration while retaining the callback-based media delivery behavior.\n- `app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/gallery/extensions/Context.kt`: Uses the coordinated GetMediaAsynctask.start(): Unit replacement launch entry point instead of AsyncTask.execute(), preserving the existing constructor arguments, callback contract, cached-media reconciliation, and background database update behavior.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- No automated test was added in this change\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`assembleDebug`)\n- [ ] Confirmed by a project maintainer\n\n## Additional context\n\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
